From a38f9516568dc83bdcaf7a0434e4bb63df3b3d1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mudb0y <stasprzecinek@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:49:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Report no done for an utterance cancelled in its last
 wait

The last flush of an utterance waits in player.idle() for the audio to
play out. A cancel from NVDA's thread stops the player, which lets that
wait go at once, and _speak then said the utterance had finished. NVDA
was told done for speech it had just silenced: the speech manager pushes
queued speech on a done when a profile trigger is pending, and a
synchronous SSML speak ends on any done.

It happened every time a cancel landed there, and the wait is the last
200 to 400 ms of every utterance, more than half of a short one such as
"OK button.". In NVDA's process on Linux, 30 cancels timed into that
wait were followed by a done 30 times. The wait and the player are the
same on Windows, so it happens there as well.

_speak now reports the end only if no cancel came. After the fix none
of the 30 was, and the next utterance still reports its own. The
watchdog, which reports an utterance it abandons in that wait itself,
is unaffected. nvda/test/engine.py holds it with a player that is
cancelled while it idles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 nvda/addon/synthDrivers/_openevv.py |  5 ++++-
 nvda/test/engine.py                 | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/nvda/addon/synthDrivers/_openevv.py b/nvda/addon/synthDrivers/_openevv.py
index e05506e..145a4bc 100644
--- a/nvda/addon/synthDrivers/_openevv.py
+++ b/nvda/addon/synthDrivers/_openevv.py
@@ -681,7 +681,10 @@ class Engine:
 		# by the next one; only the last waits for the player to run dry and
 		# says the utterance is over.
 		self._flush(last=last)
-		if last:
+		# A cancel can land while the last flush waits for the player to run
+		# dry, and stopping the player ends that wait early. The utterance did
+		# not finish then either.
+		if last and not self._discarding:
 			self._finish()
 
 	def setParam(self, which, value):
diff --git a/nvda/test/engine.py b/nvda/test/engine.py
index 1e192e9..4122a31 100644
--- a/nvda/test/engine.py
+++ b/nvda/test/engine.py
@@ -860,6 +860,18 @@ def main():
     check("an utterance ending on a mark still waits before saying done", idled, 1)
     check("and reports the mark before the done", marks, [9, None])
 
+    # A cancel from NVDA's thread while this one waits in that last idle: the
+    # stopped player lets the wait go early, and nothing finished.
+    def idleCancelled():
+        player.idled += 1
+        engine._discarding = True
+
+    player.idle = idleCancelled
+    utterance([lambda: waveform(30), lambda: index(11)])
+    del player.idle
+    engine._discarding = False
+    check("a cancel in the last wait is not followed by a done", marks, [11])
+
     # ---- cancelling, which is what crashed NVDA when it was done properly --
 
     # cancel() is the one method meant to be called from another thread, and it
